      "gap": "Third part of thm:p16-measurable-graph-examples (body 433-441: the two models Y=E xor 1{A=1/2} and Y=E have agreeing observed laws) is not argued in the declared proof: annex 986-994 asserts \"identical observed law (A,M,E)\", naming the disturbance E instead of the observed response Y, and never writes the step that P(A=1/2)=0 forces Y=E almost surely in the first model, which is the crux of the boundary example. Also unwritten in the proof: the existence of all fixed structural interventions for the singular chain (body 414; annex 935-953 treats only kernels and non-domination, with no appeal to thm:p16-measurable-interventions) and the mean-integrability premises (E|Y| finite, finite absolute response integral) required by the corollary before the four theta values are computed (annex 968-975)."
